      {
        "narration": "Astronauts spotted giant black circles stamped into Siberian lake ice. In 2009, space station photos revealed massive dark rings on Lake Baikal.",
        "visual_query": "lake baikal aerial frozen winter ice",
        "visual_fallback": "frozen lake aerial ice"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The ice was four feet thick, yet these rings stretched four miles wide. Declassified satellite images showed they had quietly appeared for decades.",
        "visual_query": "lake baikal winter ice cracks",
        "visual_fallback": "thick frozen lake ice"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Locals avoided them, fearing the lake floor was venting toxic gas. What could carve perfect miles-wide circles into solid ice?",
        "visual_query": "siberian landscape lake baikal winter",
        "visual_fallback": "snowy frozen lake shore"
      },
      {
        "narration": "In 2020, scientists lowered deep-water probes beneath the surface. They found warm underwater currents, driven by hydrothermal vents, swirling into massive thermal eddies.",
        "visual_query": "underwater thermal probe scientific research ice",
        "visual_fallback": "underwater icy freezing water"
      },
      {
        "narration": "These underwater whirlpools melt the ice from below, creating giant lens-like rings visible from space.",
        "visual_query": "lake baikal aerial ice patterns winter",
        "visual_fallback": "aerial view winter ice"
      }
